\f0\fs26\cf2 \b\fs40 How to open macdraw for the first time\b0\fs26
\par
\par
\par macOS will show \i "Apple could not verify macdraw is free of malware"\i0  because macdraw is a free, self-signed app without Apple's paid developer certificate. That message is expected - here is the one-time fix:
\par
\par
\par \b 1. Right-click\b0  the macdraw app in Applications and choose \b Open\b0 
\par \b 2. Click \b0 Open \b0 in the dialog that appears
\par \b 3. Done\b0  - double-click works normally forever after.
\par
\par
\par \b Zero-prompt alternatives\b0  (no message at all):
\par \bullet\tab Install from Terminal:
\par \f1\fs22 curl -L -o ~/Downloads/macdraw.dmg https://github.com/aadityakumarsah/macdraw/releases/latest/download/macdraw-1.0.dmg && open ~/Downloads/macdraw.dmg
\f0\fs26
\par \bullet\tab AirDrop the DMG from another Mac
\par
\par
\par Once macdraw is open, the canvas appears automatically. Draw with your mouse or trackpad, press Esc to close, and hold Control+Option to open it again.
\par
\par \cf3 macdraw - free forever, no account needed\cf2
